1702
01:15:30.930 --> 01:15:32.550
Well, Michael's going to step up.
好吧，迈克尔准备挺身而出。

1703
01:15:32.710 --> 01:15:33.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1704
01:15:33.410 --> 01:15:35.150
Because he does feel bad for her.
因为他确实为她感到难过。

1705
01:15:35.430 --> 01:15:40.170
So he goes out there, and he goes, if you don't get it, he loses it.
所以他走过去说，如果你拿不到，他就彻底失控了。

1706
01:15:40.350 --> 01:15:41.090
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1707
01:15:41.090 --> 01:15:48.290
Everyone goes in, she reads from the binder, and the look on Michael's face as she's, like, reading from the boring binder.
每个人都进去，她从文件夹里念着，迈克尔听着她像那样从那个无聊的文件夹里念着时，脸上的表情。

1708
01:15:48.510 --> 01:15:49.530
He's in love again.
他又恋爱了。

1709
01:15:49.730 --> 01:15:51.390
Well, I don't think he ever fell out of love.
嗯，我觉得他从来没不爱过。

1710
01:15:51.490 --> 01:15:52.790
They had their first spat.
他们吵了第一架。

1711
01:15:53.030 --> 01:15:54.110
I guess they did.
我想是的。

1712
01:15:54.270 --> 01:15:54.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1713
01:15:54.710 --> 01:15:56.630
Because Holly looks appreciative.
因为霍莉看起来很感激。

1714
01:15:57.090 --> 01:15:59.550
They're both like, oh, okay, we're back.
他们俩都觉得，哦，好吧，我们又好了。

1715
01:15:59.690 --> 01:16:00.690
We're going to get through this.
我们能度过难关的。

1716
01:16:00.810 --> 01:16:00.930
Yeah.
对。

1717
01:16:00.930 --> 01:16:04.090
At the very end of this episode, we have a tag.
在本集的最后，我们有一个彩蛋小片段。

1718
01:16:05.010 --> 01:16:06.350
Everyone's in the break room.
大家都待在休息室里。

1719
01:16:06.490 --> 01:16:10.050
They're eating steak that was clearly provided by Meredith.
他们在吃牛排，那显然是梅雷迪思提供的。

1720
01:16:10.570 --> 01:16:13.230
We had a fan question from Kelly W.
我们收到了来自凯莉·W的粉丝提问。

1721
01:16:13.530 --> 01:16:14.810
Okay, Kelly, what is it?
好的，凯莉，是什么问题？

1722
01:16:15.130 --> 01:16:20.410
During the last scene when everyone's eating steak in the break room, what is everyone actually eating?
在最后那个大家都坐在休息室吃牛排的场景里，大家实际上在吃什么？

1723
01:16:20.690 --> 01:16:24.370
Is it prop food or actually real expensive steak?
是道具食物还是真的昂贵牛排？

1724
01:16:24.650 --> 01:16:25.790
And Savi A.
萨维·A

1725
01:16:26.130 --> 01:16:29.850
wants to know, Angela, what were you eating since your character is a vegetarian?
想知道，安吉拉，既然你的角色是个素食主义者，你当时在吃什么？

1726
01:16:29.850 --> 01:16:31.610
I was eating potatoes.
我在吃土豆。

1727
01:16:31.970 --> 01:16:33.270
That's what it looked like to me.
我看着就觉得是那样。

1728
01:16:33.550 --> 01:16:34.350
I was eating potatoes.
我当时在吃土豆。

1729
01:16:34.510 --> 01:16:35.570
That's something we thought about.
这是我们考虑过的事情。

1730
01:16:36.010 --> 01:16:42.130
One of the things that Peter and Vartan shared is that our prop food was amazingly good food.
彼得和瓦尔坦分享的一点是，我们的道具食物是出奇的好吃的食物。

1731
01:16:42.270 --> 01:16:42.670
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1732
01:16:42.870 --> 01:16:45.610
That they didn't give us, like, kind of crappy food to eat in scenes.
他们没有在拍摄时给我们那种很烂的食物吃。

1733
01:16:46.070 --> 01:16:53.550
And Peter and Vartan would work with props, but I would have to think that Phil Shea and his team got us really good food from a restaurant.
而且彼得和瓦尔坦会负责道具，但我猜菲尔·希亚和他的团队从餐馆给我们弄来了非常好的食物。

1734
01:16:53.770 --> 01:16:55.250
That was going to be my guess.
我也会这么猜。

1735
01:16:55.510 --> 01:16:57.810
Whenever I ate food in a scene, it was delicious.
每当我在场景里吃东西时，它都美味极了。

1736
01:16:58.190 --> 01:16:58.470
Yeah.
对。

1737
01:16:58.470 --> 01:17:01.450
So it was probably some really good steak.
所以那可能是一些非常棒的牛排。

1738
01:17:01.690 --> 01:17:01.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1739
01:17:02.130 --> 01:17:03.210
What a day at work.
多么棒的工作日啊。

1740
01:17:03.350 --> 01:17:07.030
Hey, guys, come in and eat these steak and ribs for an hour.
嘿，伙计们，进来吃一个小时的牛排和排骨吧。

1741
01:17:07.530 --> 01:17:08.690
Angela, you can have these potatoes.
安吉拉，你可以吃这些土豆。

1742
01:17:09.010 --> 01:17:09.870
Sorry, Ange.
对不起，安琪。

1743
01:17:10.930 --> 01:17:12.410
Well, there you have it.
好了，答案就在这里。

1744
01:17:12.530 --> 01:17:13.910
That's business ethics.
这就是商业道德。

1745
01:17:14.290 --> 01:17:14.570
Yeah.
没错。

1746
01:17:14.830 --> 01:17:16.550
Thank you so much to Amy Ryan.
非常感谢艾米·莱恩。

1747
01:17:16.870 --> 01:17:21.890
And thank you to James O'Kerry for giving me the lowdown on Coopers.
也感谢詹姆斯·奥凯里向我透露库珀斯的内幕。

1748
01:17:21.890 --> 01:17:29.250
And thank you to BJ Novak for pitching Peter and Vartan and Sergio and Alan to do the DVD commentary.
还要感谢B·J·诺瓦克邀请彼得、瓦尔坦、塞尔吉奥和艾伦来做DVD评论音轨。

1749
01:17:29.550 --> 01:17:30.750
That was just so wonderful.
那真是太棒了。

1750
01:17:31.210 --> 01:17:34.730
If you guys love the show, you'll love these commentaries.
如果你们喜欢这部剧，你们一定会喜欢这些评论音轨。

1751
01:17:35.150 --> 01:17:39.010
Well, I think, on that note, you might go have a volcano.
好吧，我想基于这一点，你们可能会去喝一杯“火山”鸡尾酒。

1752
01:17:39.010 --> 01:17:48.870
And I hope all of you guys have some hardcore love in your life for approximately 19 minutes or an average of six minutes.
我希望你们所有人在生活中都能拥有大约19分钟，或者平均6分钟的炽热爱情。

1753
01:17:49.330 --> 01:17:50.470
That would be fine.
那就挺好的。

1754
01:17:51.610 --> 01:17:52.730
See you next week.
我们下周见。

1755
01:17:52.770 --> 01:17:53.290
Bye, guys.
再见，各位。

1756
01:17:53.290 --> 01:18:00.370
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies' Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士》的“第二杯”节目。

1757
